# Code quality

Recruiters will read this repo. Write the change a careful engineer would merge.

- TypeScript strict. No `any`. Narrow at the boundary.
- Simple and readable. No extra abstractions or wrappers for a single call site.
- Follow existing structure. Change as little as possible.
- Empty, invalid, and failed lookups are first-class UI, not `console.error`.
- Colocate helpers next to the only caller. Do not invent a util/framework layer for one use. UI belongs in the atomic layers — see `atomic-design.mdc` and `composability.mdc`.

```ts
// ❌
function getData(id: any) {
  try { return fetchTx(id) } catch (e) {}
}

// ✅
async function getTransaction(hash: `0x${string}`): Promise<Transaction> {
  return fetchTransaction(hash)
}
```
